# Pairs with StaleEpochNeverAppends. A claim written before L's clear is raised
# after it. The clear deleted the entry, so a raise checked against the entries
# alone accepts an epoch the clear retired, and its activation appends. The shard
# does not check the floor on appends (#5635), so the raise's floor check is the
# guard. Production holds the leaf's gate across a claim's write and raise, so
# L's own clear cannot fall between them; the model allows it (an
# over-approximation), and another leaf's retirement can.
MODULE: StaleEpochNeverAppendsIgnoresRetiredFloor
TARGET: StaleEpochNeverAppends
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the claim's raise is not refused at or below the retired floor
PERTURBS: ClaimRaise

--- FIND
    /\ epoch[a] >= Max2(fence, memFence)
    /\ epoch[a] > retired
--- REPLACE
    /\ epoch[a] >= Max2(fence, memFence)
\* MUTATION: the retired floor is not checked at the raise.
--- END
